The checkout step declares fetch-depth 0 because the changelog gate's shallow-history refusal rejects any checkout it cannot confirm is unshallow, and the action's undeclared default depth of 1 would otherwise make CI refuse every commit; removing this depth setting or loosening the refusal reopens the shallow-clone hole this pairing exists to close.
